# Glow & Go — Antigravity Instructions

Read `AGENTS.md` and `PROGRESS.md` at the start of each coding session. `AGENTS.md` is the canonical set of project, architecture, safety, security, quality, and Git workflow rules. Follow those instructions rather than duplicating or overriding them here.

Before edits: summarize the verified repository state and ONE proposed milestone; list files to create/edit and how to verify success. Do not assume the user knows setup steps.

During edits: stay within the approved milestone, keep React `client/` separate from Express `server/`, avoid secrets in frontend or commits, and do not silently install dependencies, push, or deploy.

After edits: report changes and actual checks, ask permission before commit/push/deploy, then update `PROGRESS.md` with facts, blockers, and the next step. Do not claim unverified tasks are complete.

Note: this file is only effective if the current coding agent is configured to load `.antigravityrules`; `AGENTS.md` is the portable primary instructions file.
